  "notes": [
    "Irregular -ER verb — the *c* changes to *zc* before *o* and *a*: irregular only in the yo form of Presente (*aparezco*, not *apareco*) and throughout Subjuntivo Presente (*aparezca, aparezcas...*). All other tenses are fully regular.",
    "Same pattern as *nacer*, *conocer*, and its own opposite *desaparecer*",
    "Past participle: *aparecido* (regular)",
    "Means \"to appear\" or \"to show up\" — *apareció de repente* (he/she suddenly appeared), *el documento apareció en el cajón* (the document turned up in the drawer)",
    "Related: *aparición* (appearance, apparition), *apariencia* (appearance, looks), *desaparecer* (to disappear — opposite)"
  ],
